# Metric health and propagation foundation

Status: **Phase 006 is active. Group 01 is accepted with HLTH-001–HLTH-008.**

Preserve permanently:

- successful load/run ≠ healthy produced table;
- available statistic ≠ useful metric;
- metric definition ≠ metric Observation ≠ Assessment;
- metric existence ≠ normative threshold;
- threshold authority ≠ metric statistical meaning;
- Baseline range ≠ normative Expectation;
- local metric ≠ propagated metric ≠ derived reconciliation expectation;
- technical metric view ≠ separate business truth;
- upstream anomaly ≠ downstream failure;
- metric used for monitoring ≠ automatically safe for Execution Gate control;
- richer/expensive metric ≠ synchronous production-path requirement;
- semantic applicability ≠ profile selection ≠ source support ≠ current availability ≠ health outcome;
- `not applicable`, `not selected`, `unsupported`, `unavailable`, `pending`, and `pass` are distinct;
- same metric display name ≠ same definition/version when formula/denominator/grain/population semantics materially change.

Accepted Phase 006 Group 01 foundation:

- Define purposeful per-asset metric profiles rather than calculating every possible statistic.
- Distinguish core operational/table, critical-field/business, transformation-specific reconciliation, and diagnostic/on-demand profile roles.
- Canonical metric families are operational/output, temporal/freshness, structural/schema, volume/population, completeness/missingness, uniqueness/key integrity, validity/domain, distribution/shape, relational/transformation integrity, and business-semantic measurement.
- Metric applicability depends on semantic role, data type, grain, transformation, criticality/context, consumer use and definition version.
- Avoid meaningless metrics such as quantiles for opaque identifiers or universal column-level statistics without an identified failure mode/use.
- Material metric/check Observations retain definition/version, subject/window/grain/population, source/input evidence, temporal provenance, approximation/sampling/coverage limitations and restriction status.
- Diagnostic/on-demand evaluation does not automatically promote a metric to routine profile membership.

Later Phase 006 rules still to be refined:

- Group 02 — structural/schema/DDL compatibility;
- Group 03 — Baseline comparability, distributions, seasonality/cohorts, low-volume/sample-size behavior;
- Group 04 — thresholds/margins/warning/failure/waiver Assessment semantics;
- Group 05 — selective transformation-aware propagation/reconciliation;
- Group 06 — composite health and progressive result timing/control-suitability;
- Group 07 — consolidation/exit.

Cross-phase boundaries:

- Phase 005 decides metric/Expectation/threshold authority and disclosure governance.
- Phase 006 defines metric and health semantics.
- Phase 007 refines Lineage-aware propagation/operational use.
- Phase 009 evaluates actual source support, cost, latency and retention.
- Phase 010 selects computation/storage/fast-path architecture.

Do not recursively cascade every upstream statistic through Lineage. Do not force monitoring metrics onto the production critical path unless an explicitly accepted high-consequence control requires them and the later evidence/timing criteria are satisfied.
